# A companion (Docs/Design/83-dialogue-trees.md, Phase 3): Talk with a resident travelling in the party (doc 32). The
# party's orders as words (follow, wait, go home, part ways: Game::orderCompanion, which they answer in their own
# words, and the conversation ends), how they're holding up, what they think (doc 84, Phase 12), goodbye. The wheel
# keeps the orders too.

tree companion
for here.companion=yes
priority 4
entry talk hub
entry orders hub

node hub
say Yes? | What is it? | Lead on, or are we stopping?
say[here.waiting=yes] Still here. Moving on? | I've kept my place. What now?
free
choice Follow me. [here.waiting=yes] -> do order follow ; refused refused
choice Wait here for me. [here.waiting=no] -> do order wait ; refused refused
choice How are you holding up? -> holding
choice What do you think? -> think
choice Go home for now. -> do order home ; refused refused
choice We part ways here. -> do order dismiss ; refused refused
choice Something else... -> do open chat
choice Goodbye. -> bye

node holding
say Well enough. Lead on. | I'm fine. Don't fuss.
say[tired=yes] Tired. We could rest a while. | My legs are done in.
say[injured=light] A few scrapes. Nothing to stop for.
say[injured=bad priority=2] I'm hurt, badly. I need to rest.
free
choice Follow me. [here.waiting=yes] -> do order follow ; refused refused
choice Wait here for me. [here.waiting=no] -> do order wait ; refused refused
choice Goodbye. -> bye

# "What do you think?" (Docs/Design/84 §13.1.6, Phase 12): once said in chat to a companion and answered there; now
# here, answered by the game from the companion's own stances (Game::companionOpinion: their view on one of the realm's
# issues, the library's opinion lines, their mantle's first). These words where they have no view to give.
node think
ask companion.opinion
say Hard to say. I'll think on it. | I've no strong view either way. | I'd sooner keep my thoughts to myself, for now.
free
choice How are you holding up? -> holding
choice Goodbye. -> bye

node refused
say #topic.why#
choice Goodbye. -> bye

node bye
say Right. | Lead on. | As you like.
end
